    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334">

                <pb facs="0463" n="395" xml:id="pg395"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Clay to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 152.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">LeGation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg, Russia</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 28, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Admiral Farragut, with four ships, has been
                    here now three weeks, and sails Friday for Stockholm.</p>
                <p>He has been received everywhere, from the grand admiral, the Grand Duke
                    Constantine down to the lowest peasant, with respect and true cordiality. Last
                    night a grand ball was given him and the American officers, at the house of the
                    governor of Cronstadt, Vice-Admiral Lessoffky, at which the minister of marine,
                    Admiral Croblie, and all the distinguished officers of the Russian fleet were
                    present. The impression produced here by the American fleet and its gentle manly
                    officers has been most favorable.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. M. CLAY.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
